   "subject": "Plot the same tree side by side?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, <div><br></div><div>If you generated a tree using:</div><div><br></div><div><div>   library(ggtree)</div><div>   set.seed(123)<br></div><div>   tree &lt;- rtree(30)<br></div><div>   ggtree(tree, branch.length = &quot;none&quot;) + geom_tiplab()<br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Would it be possible to plot the same tree side by side, similar to the attached image?</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to map two different character states in the form of pie charts onto the nodes of the same tree, but when I have done this it looks quite cluttered. I thought presenting the results with the same tree side by side and different characters for each might be a better way of presenting this. </div><div><br></div><div>Hope this makes sense </div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>Ollie</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
